WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.020
One of the beautiful things about looting
and rioting is that it just immediately makes

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:05.340
people's lives better.

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:09.600
They get things that they would otherwise
have to work for weeks or months to get,

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:10.759
they get them in an instant.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:15.520
The writer and activist Vicky Osterweil is
the latest and most strident defender

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:20.020
of the violence and destruction that's accompanied
more than three months of protests

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.620
following the death of George Floyd.

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:27.680
Osterweil argues that in the last years of
Martin Luther King Jr's life, as his focus

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:32.720
moved beyond desegregation and voting rights
and towards promoting socialism,

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:37.000
he had a change of heart about looting and destruction
as a tool for social change.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.080
Though he wasn't calling for violent revolution
she writes,

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:44.060
neither was he chastising or rejecting rioters anymore.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:46.580
Others have pointed to the famous King line.

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:55.620
In reality, King was unwavering in his commitment
to nonviolence.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:01:02.340
Every summer we're going to have this kind
of vigorous protest, my hope is

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:04.280
that it will be nonviolent.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:10.460
I would hope that we can avoid riots because
riots are self-defeating and socially destructive.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:15.710
He tried to make his position crystal clear
in that same 1966 interview with 60 minutes

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:17.070
Mike Wallace.

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:27.410
I will never change in my basic idea that
nonviolence is the most potent weapon available

00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:30.400
to the Negro in his struggle for freedom and
justice.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.740
And less than a year before his death King
delivered a lecture addressing skeptics

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:37.920
of nonviolence following the 1967 riots.

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:44.820
Many people feel that nonviolence as a strategy
for social change was cremated in the flames

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:48.140
of the urban riots of the last two years.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:54.000
Yet King doubled down, calling for massive
sustained nonviolent civil disobedience.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:02:00.780
In this world nonviolence is no longer an
option for intellectual analysis.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:04.500
It is an imperative for action.

00:02:04.509 --> 00:02:10.610
King considered violent protests to be self-defeating
because as he argued in 1968, every time a

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:16.220
riot develops it makes a right wing takeover
more likely, and helps the segregationist

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:17.500
George Wallace.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:23.220
Vicky Osterweil writes admiringly of the nationwide
riots that followed King's assassination as

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:49.280
But the Princeton political scientist Omar
Wasow has studied the '68 riots in detail,

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:54.069
finding that they allowed Richard Nixon to
beat Democrat Hubert Humphrey in that year's

00:02:54.069 --> 00:02:55.470
presidential race.

00:02:55.470 --> 00:03:00.810
As King understood, media coverage was why
looting and violence backfired.

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:06.280
When protesters engaged in violence that predicted
a headline about riots tomorrow, a headline

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:11.330
that was much more likely to focus on crime
and disorder, and public opinion moves very

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:12.420
closely with that.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:17.870
So when the newspapers are talking about civil
rights, civil rights becomes the most important

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:20.220
problem in public opinion surveys.

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:25.019
And when newspapers are heavily covering crime
and riots, crime and riots become the thing

00:03:25.019 --> 00:03:26.590
that is the most important problem.

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:32.629
And so the tactics that are employed by protesters
can really make a powerful impact on how the

00:03:32.629 --> 00:03:35.739
media tell the story, which in turn shapes
public opinion.

00:03:35.739 --> 00:03:41.100
Some media outlets have opted to downplay
the violence and destruction, but King's warning

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:47.050
and Wasow's research still resonate today
as polls show a sharp downward turn in approval

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:52.260
ratings of the Black Lives Matter Movement
in recent weeks, especially in swing states

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:55.720
like Wisconsin, even before riots hit Kenosha.

00:03:55.720 --> 00:04:01.739
Democratic presidential candidate Joe Biden
seems to fundamentally understand that.

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:05.700
Rioting is not protesting, looting is not
protesting.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:10.240
Which might help explain how he's maintained
the lead so far against an incumbent who's

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:13.100
often fanned the flames with his rhetoric.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:18.400
If a city or a state refuses to take the actions
that are necessary to defend the life and

00:04:18.409 --> 00:04:25.900
property of their residents, then I will deploy
the United States Military and quickly solve

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:27.380
the problem for them.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:37.780
When King said this he wasn't excusing riots,
but imploring observers to acknowledge the

00:04:37.789 --> 00:04:42.770
unjust conditions that contributed to their
emergence in the first place.

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:51.800
Certain conditions continue to exist in our
society, which must be condemned as vigorously

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.300
as we condemn riots.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:57.800
Rioters and looters are at the core of all
of these movements.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:03.569
The paths forward to social change couldn't
be more clear, persistent nonviolent resistance

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:09.939
as practiced by Martin Luther King, Jr. who
helped achieve historic civil rights legislation,

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:15.700
or rioting and looting, promoted by activists
who believe we need to argue and defend

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:22.620
every tactic that might help us overturn this miserable
world of white supremacy, anti-blackness,

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:26.940
cisheteropatriarchy, capitalism, empire, and property.

